S|Thanks for joining, David. Before we talk numbers, how has the quarter gone for your team?
D|Busy, honestly. Volume is up twenty percent, and the reporting dashboard has been really useful.
S|That's great to hear. You mentioned last time that onboarding new staff was slow.
D|Yes. We would like two more training sessions in January, ideally remote.
S|We can include those in the renewal at no extra cost. I will confirm dates with our training team.
D|Perfect. The other question is data retention. Legal wants us to keep records for seven years.
S|Our standard plan keeps five years. Seven years is an add on, and I will send you the pricing.
D|Please do. If the numbers work, we can sign before the end of the month.
S|Great. So my actions are the training dates and the retention pricing, both by Friday.
S|Before you go, should we invite your operations lead to the training sessions as well?
D|Yes, please add her. She will want to see the new reporting features.
D|And I will get sign off from our legal team. Talk soon.
